---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Default.astro';
import { DrawerShowcase } from '../../components/molecules/DrawerShowcase.jsx';
---

<Layout title="Drawer" section="molecules/drawer">
  <h1 class="page-title">Drawer</h1>
  <p class="page-sub">Slide-in panel for filters, inspectors, and secondary flows · side and bottom placements</p>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Overview</span>
      <span class="section-desc">When and why to use a drawer</span>
    </div>

    <p>
      The Drawer molecule provides a modal-like panel that slides in from the side or bottom of the viewport.
      Use it for secondary surfaces such as filters, inspectors, and composition flows where the main page
      should remain visible as context. For primary tasks that fully capture attention, prefer the Modal
      molecule instead.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Showcase</span>
      <span class="section-desc">Typical catalogue filter pattern</span>
    </div>
    <div class="showcase-wrap">
      <DrawerShowcase client:load />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Header & footer behaviour</span>
      <span class="section-desc">Fixed header band and sticky actions</span>
    </div>

    <p>
      The Drawer header keeps a compact 80px band for the title and subtitle only, separated from
      the content by a subtle divider. The body scrolls independently when content overflows, while
      the action bar stays pinned to the bottom with its own top border. This keeps primary actions
      visible even in long forms without hiding the surrounding page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="footer">Nexus Design System · Drawer</div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .showcase-wrap {
    background: var(--card-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-100);
    padding: var(--space-300);
  }
</style>

